    "created_at": "2020-06-11T14:05:52Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-06-11T14:05:52Z",
    "body": "I still don't understand. You shouldn't be changing `input.validity`, which indicates that `input.value` is invalid, if `input.value` doesn't change.\r\n\r\nIt sounds like Chrome has a bug here (either in changing `input.validity` too early, or not changing `input.value` to the empty string when invalid values are entered). To address that we shouldn't introduce some new event. Chrome should fix its date control so that `value` and `validity` stay synchronized, as the specification requires.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
