    "created_at": "2020-06-11T18:04:23Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-06-11T18:04:23Z",
    "body": "Where does the spec say that `input.validity` can only change when `input.value` changes? I had a hard time searching.\r\n\r\nI also took a look at number inputs, and they actually have the desired behavior: When an incomplete value is entered, `input.validity` changes to show that it isn't valid, and an `input` event is fired, despite the fact that `input.value` never changed: https://jsfiddle.net/jarhar/jm60zydb/\r\nGiven that chrome, firefox, and safari all have this behavior, maybe we should change the spec to say that the `input` event can be fired when `input.validity` changes.\r\n\r\nHowever, I also just noticed that number inputs will fire the `input` event every time you enter another character even when it doesn't change `input.validity`... so it wouldn't be correct to say that the current behavior for number inputs is that they fire `input` every time `input.validity` or `input.value` changes. This behavior is also present in chrome, firefox, and safari.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
