    "updated_at": "2020-06-11T18:10:25Z",
    "body": "> When an incomplete value is entered, input.validity changes to show that it isn't valid, and an input event is fired, despite the fact that input.value never changed: https://jsfiddle.net/jarhar/jm60zydb/\r\n\r\nThe test suggested there isn't quite right. What you want to do is enter a valid value, e.g. `5`, then make it invalid, e.g. by typing `e`. You'll see that `input.value` changes at the same time as `input.validity`.",
